From e07c3127770a9952c78f130507a4d85104f4a1dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 18:31:48 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 34/39] v4.8-gpu: drop the dead stats row and fix the RT label

The GPU stats section carried a ">> lock contention" row hardcoded to
zero with no backing counter -- dead data that also misaligned the GPU
row indices.  Remove it and reindex the remaining rows.  The RT throttle
row note said "FIFO rogue demotions"; the valve never demotes, it
requeues within the RT class, so the note now reads "FIFO rogue
requeues".

Signed-off-by: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
---
 kernel/sched/infinity_sched.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kernel/sched/infinity_sched.c b/kernel/sched/infinity_sched.c
index 49a598edb..18bb9c58f 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/infinity_sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/infinity_sched.c
@@ -325,7 +325,7 @@ static int infinity_stats_proc_handler(const struct ctl_table *ctl, int write,
 	/* ---- RT rows ---- */
 	rt_rows[0].label = "RT throttles";
 	fill_pretty_llu(rt_rows[0].value, sizeof(rt_rows[0].value), rtc);
-	strscpy(rt_rows[0].note, "FIFO rogue demotions",
+	strscpy(rt_rows[0].note, "FIFO rogue requeues",
 		sizeof(rt_rows[0].note));
 
 	/* ---- GPU rows ---- */
-- 
2.55.0

